title: 'cumulus: fix V3 scheduling parent picking'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    A V3 candidate takes its scheduling parent by walking back from the relay
    chain best block until a slot older than the one being produced for. That
    walk read the wall clock a second time to decide which slot that was. The
    slot timer wakes 2ms before the slot it reports begins, so the second read
    still returned the previous slot. The walk then stepped one block too far
    back, anchoring the candidate at an older relay block than the slot intended.
    The production slot is now passed down from the slot timer and used as the
    only source of truth for the walk.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: minor
